From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:46:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 51/52] mount-utils: grow UFS and ext file systems on FreeBSD

FreeBSD built resizefs_unsupported.go, so every in-tree file system
expansion (local PVs on a raw block device, NodeExpand for volumes the
kubelet formats) failed with "Resize is not supported for this build".

resizefs_freebsd.go grows UFS with growfs(8), which works while the file
system is mounted, and ext2/3/4 with resize2fs from e2fsprogs. FreeBSD
has no online ext resize: resize2fs on a mounted ext volume fails with
EPERM opening the device, and that error is returned. NeedResize
compares diskinfo(8)'s media size with the UFS size from dumpfs(8)
(size fragments * fsize) and skips read-only mounts (statfs MNT_RDONLY).

TestSafeFormatAndMount expected the Linux fsck -a and mkfs.xfs -f; on
FreeBSD the formatter runs e2fsck -p and mkfs.xfs, so the expected
commands are mapped (the test panicked and aborted the package's tests).
Also gofmt mount_freebsd.go.
